How to Run Examples:
--------------------
1. Verify Python is installed
python3 --version

2. Verify the `venv` module is available
python3 -m venv --help

If it is not available:
sudo apt update
sudo apt install python3-venv

3. Navigate to the project directory
cd python-learning-journey

4. Create a virtual environment
python3 -m venv .venv

5. Activate the virtual environment
source .venv/bin/activate

If your prompt changes to something similar to:
(.venv) user@host:~/python-learning-journey$

the virtual environment is active.

6. Install project dependencies (if applicable)
Example: pip install pygame requests

7. Run any example
python 01_variables/example1.py

8. Deactivate the virtual environment
deactivate

Note: Every example in this repository is designed to be run independently. 
Execute the programs, observe the output, and experiment by modifying the code to reinforce each concept.


 
                                                                 
